% Parenteral Nutrition: LCD L38953 and its Policy Article A58836 (DME MACs).
% A policy program of the DMEPOS model: it includes dmepos.le (orders,
% delivery, benefit category, continued need, refills) and
% enteral_nutrition.le (whose template for a stay covered by Part A it
% reads) and states when a claim for a parenteral nutrient, a supply
% allowance or an infusion pump is REASONABLE AND NECESSARY:
%   the coverage criteria of every item — the treating practitioner has
%   documented that enteral nutrition was considered and ruled out, tried
%   and found ineffective, or exacerbates gastrointestinal tract
%   dysfunction; the beneficiary has (a) a condition involving the small
%   intestine and/or its exocrine glands which significantly impairs the
%   absorption of nutrients or (b) a motility disorder of the stomach
%   and/or intestine which impairs the transport and absorption of
%   nutrients; the treating practitioner evaluated the beneficiary within
%   30 days before parenteral nutrition began, or documented why not and
%   the other monitoring methods used;
%   the nutrients (the homemix components B4164, B4168, B4172, B4176,
%   B4178, B4180, B4185, B4187, B4216; the premix solutions B4189, B4193,
%   B4197, B4199; the special formulas B5000, B5100, B5200): a caloric
%   intake of 20-35 cal/kg/day, a protein order of 0.8-2.0 gm/kg/day for the
%   amino acids, a dextrose concentration of at least 10% for the
%   carbohydrates, lipids within the FDA-approved dosing — each outside its
%   range only with the practitioner's documented medical necessity (a
%   finding) — and the special formulas with the documented condition and
%   need;
%   the supply allowances (B4220, B4222) and the administration kit (B4224),
%   one a day;
%   the infusion pumps (B9004, B9006), except when the nutrition is given in
%   an outpatient facility.
% The benefit is the Prosthetic Device benefit (Policy Article A58836,
% Social Security Act §1861(s)(8)), which carries no condition on the place
% of use.
%
% The payment conditions the Article adds (section remedy): the test of
% permanence — in the treating practitioner's judgment the impairment will
% be of long and indefinite duration (the LCD states "The beneficiary must
% have a permanent impairment" and refers to the Article, whose test it is:
% a benefit condition, as in the other nutrition, ostomy and urological
% policies of the model); no stay covered by Part A; and the dispensing cap
% of the LCD, a one-month quantity at a time (the pump is not a supply). The
% supply allowances are daily allowances to which the refill requirements do
% not apply: a claim for one is never marked a refill.
%
% How the criteria are read. What the record states is a scenario fact: the
% condition (a) or (b) in the LCD's words, the dates of the evaluation and of
% the start of parenteral nutrition, the reason documented for a late
% evaluation, the caloric intake, protein and dextrose concentration
% ordered (numbers, so the ranges are in the rules), a lipid use above the
% FDA-approved dosing, the outpatient facility, the stay. One a day is read
% with a month of 31 days. The findings this policy reads (the judged
% template of dmepos.le), and the criterion each stands for:
%   permanent gastrointestinal impairment (the Article's test of
%   permanence; enteral_nutrition.le reads it under the same name);
%   enteral nutrition unsuitable (ONE finding for the three alternatives:
%   "enteral nutrition has been considered and ruled out , tried and been
%   found ineffective, or that EN exacerbates gastrointestinal tract
%   dysfunction");
%   atypical caloric intake necessary, atypical protein order necessary, low
%   dextrose concentration necessary, excess lipid dosing necessary (the
%   practitioner "must document the medical necessity" of an order outside
%   the range — each consulted only when the record's numbers are outside
%   it);
%   special parenteral nutrient necessary (B5000, B5100, B5200: "The
%   beneficiary’s medical record must adequately document the specific
%   condition and the necessity for the special nutrient").
%
% Not modelled: "Only one infusion pump is covered" (the claims of two pumps
% would both be read); one supply kit and one administration kit a day
% beyond each claim's own count; the IV pole E0776 and its BA modifier; the
% miscellaneous code B9999; the coding of premix against homemix components
% (no separate billing of carbohydrates, amino acids or additives with a
% premix); the units of service against the order, the DIF of claims before
% 2023, the KX, GA, GY and GZ modifiers; the home administration services.
% The Article says it lists ICD-10 codes, but no table of them is in
% sources/icd10.

the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    % the record
    *a beneficiary* has a condition of the small intestine or its exocrine glands significantly impairing the absorption of nutrients; undefined.
    *a beneficiary* has a motility disorder of the stomach or intestine impairing the transport or absorption of nutrients by the gastrointestinal system; undefined.
    parenteral nutrition of *a beneficiary* was initiated on *a date*; undefined.
    the treating practitioner saw *a beneficiary* to evaluate the parenteral nutrition needs on *a date*; undefined.
    the treating practitioner documented the reason for the late evaluation of *a beneficiary* with the other monitoring methods used; undefined.
    the caloric intake ordered for *a beneficiary* is *a number* cal per kg per day; undefined.
    the protein ordered for *a beneficiary* is *a number* gm per kg per day; undefined.
    the dextrose concentration ordered for *a beneficiary* is *a number* percent; undefined.
    the lipid use of *a beneficiary* exceeds the FDA approved dosing recommendations; undefined.
    *a beneficiary* receives the parenteral nutrition in an outpatient facility; undefined.
    % derived
    *a beneficiary* meets the parenteral nutrition coverage criteria.
    *a beneficiary* has a parenteral nutrition qualifying condition.
    the evaluation before parenteral nutrition is documented for *a beneficiary*.
    *an item* is a parenteral nutrient.
    the caloric intake of *a beneficiary* is justified.
    the nutrient order of *an item* is justified for *a beneficiary*.
    the protein order of *a beneficiary* is justified.
    the dextrose concentration of *a beneficiary* is justified.
    the lipid dose of *a beneficiary* is justified.
    *a claim* is within one parenteral supply allowance a day.
    *a claim* is within the dispensing limit for parenteral nutrition.

the knowledge base parenteral_nutrition includes these resources:
    dmepos,
    enteral_nutrition.

the knowledge base parenteral_nutrition includes:

LCD L38953 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/lcd.aspx?lcdid=38953".
the text of LCD L38953 is at "sources/lcd/L38953.txt".
Policy Article A58836 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/article.aspx?articleid=58836".
the text of Policy Article A58836 is at "sources/article/A58836.txt".

% The nutrients, by code (the Article's coding guidelines).
rule pn_nutrient_codes with provenance Policy Article A58836,
        confer "When homemix parenteral nutrition solutions are used, the component carbohydrates (B4164, B4180), amino acids (B4168, B4172, B4176, B4178), additives (B4216), and lipids (B4185 or B4187) are all separately billable":
an item is a parenteral nutrient
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["B4164", "B4168", "B4172", "B4176", "B4178", "B4180", "B4185", "B4187", "B4216", "B4189", "B4193", "B4197", "B4199", "B5000", "B5100", "B5200"].

% The codes this policy decides — outside the section checklist: a claim
% of another policy fails here without failing its own applicability.
% The codes this policy decides, and their benefit: the Prosthetic Device
% benefit (Policy Article A58836), with no condition on the place of use.
rule pn_codes with provenance Policy Article A58836,
        confer "Parenteral Nutrition is covered under the Prosthetic Device benefit (Social Security Act § 1861(s)(8))":
the policy for code a code is parenteral_nutrition
    if the code is in ["B4164", "B4168", "B4172", "B4176", "B4178", "B4180", "B4185", "B4187", "B4216", "B4189", "B4193", "B4197", "B4199", "B5000", "B5100", "B5200", "B4220", "B4222", "B4224", "B9004", "B9006"].

section applicability is:

rule pn_benefit with provenance Policy Article A58836,
        confer "Parenteral Nutrition is covered under the Prosthetic Device benefit (Social Security Act § 1861(s)(8))":
the benefit category of code a code is prosthetic devices
    if the policy for code the code is parenteral_nutrition.

section question is:

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% The coverage criteria of every item.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule pn_criteria with provenance LCD L38953,
        confer "For parenteral nutrition to be considered reasonable and necessary, the treating practitioner must document that enteral nutrition has been considered and ruled out , tried and been found ineffective, or that EN exacerbates gastrointestinal tract dysfunction":
a beneficiary meets the parenteral nutrition coverage criteria
    if the finding enteral nutrition unsuitable about the beneficiary is established
    and the beneficiary has a parenteral nutrition qualifying condition
    and the evaluation before parenteral nutrition is documented for the beneficiary.

rule pn_condition_absorption with provenance LCD L38953,
        confer "a condition involving the small intestine and/or its exocrine glands which significantly impairs the absorption of nutrients":
a beneficiary has a parenteral nutrition qualifying condition
    if the beneficiary has a condition of the small intestine or its exocrine glands significantly impairing the absorption of nutrients.

rule pn_condition_motility with provenance LCD L38953,
        confer "disease of the stomach and/or intestine which is a motility disorder and impairs the ability of nutrients to be transported through and absorbed by the gastrointestinal (GI) system":
a beneficiary has a parenteral nutrition qualifying condition
    if the beneficiary has a motility disorder of the stomach or intestine impairing the transport or absorption of nutrients by the gastrointestinal system.

% within the 30 days before the start, otherwise the documented reason and
% the other monitoring
rule pn_evaluation with provenance LCD L38953,
        confer "If the treating practitioner does not see the beneficiary within this timeframe, they must document the reason why and describe what other monitoring methods were used to evaluate the beneficiary's parenteral nutrition needs":
the evaluation before parenteral nutrition is documented for a beneficiary
    if parenteral nutrition of the beneficiary was initiated on a date
    and the treating practitioner saw the beneficiary to evaluate the parenteral nutrition needs on an other date
    and the date is a number days after the other date
    and the number >= 0
    and the number <= 30
    otherwise the treating practitioner documented the reason for the late evaluation of the beneficiary with the other monitoring methods used.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% The nutrients: the ranges of the order, the special formulas.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule pn_nutrient_claim with provenance LCD L38953,
        confer "If the coverage requirements for parenteral nutritional therapy are met under the prosthetic device benefit provision, related supplies, equipment and nutrients are also covered":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is a parenteral nutrient
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary meets the parenteral nutrition coverage criteria
    and the caloric intake of the beneficiary is justified
    and the nutrient order of the item is justified for the beneficiary.

rule pn_calories with provenance LCD L38953,
        confer "A total caloric daily intake of 20-35 cal/kg/day is considered reasonable and necessary to achieve or maintain appropriate body weight. The treating practitioner must document the medical necessity for a caloric intake outside this range in an individual beneficiary":
the caloric intake of a beneficiary is justified
    if the caloric intake ordered for the beneficiary is a number cal per kg per day
    and the number >= 20
    and the number <= 35
    otherwise the finding atypical caloric intake necessary about the beneficiary is established.

rule pn_amino_acids with provenance LCD L38953,
        confer "The treating practitioner must document the medical necessity for protein orders outside of the range of 0.8-2.0 gm/kg/day (B4168, B4172, B4176, B4178)":
the nutrient order of an item is justified for a beneficiary
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["B4168", "B4172", "B4176", "B4178"]
    and the protein order of the beneficiary is justified.

rule pn_protein_range with provenance LCD L38953,
        confer "The treating practitioner must document the medical necessity for protein orders outside of the range of 0.8-2.0 gm/kg/day (B4168, B4172, B4176, B4178)":
the protein order of a beneficiary is justified
    if the protein ordered for the beneficiary is a number gm per kg per day
    and the number >= 0.8
    and the number <= 2.0
    otherwise the finding atypical protein order necessary about the beneficiary is established.

rule pn_carbohydrates with provenance LCD L38953,
        confer "dextrose concentration less than 10":
the nutrient order of an item is justified for a beneficiary
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["B4164", "B4180"]
    and the dextrose concentration of the beneficiary is justified.

rule pn_dextrose_range with provenance LCD L38953,
        confer "dextrose concentration less than 10":
the dextrose concentration of a beneficiary is justified
    if the dextrose concentration ordered for the beneficiary is a number percent
    and the number >= 10
    otherwise the finding low dextrose concentration necessary about the beneficiary is established.

rule pn_lipids with provenance LCD L38953,
        confer "lipid use per month in excess of the product-specific, FDA-approved dosing recommendations (B4185, B4187)":
the nutrient order of an item is justified for a beneficiary
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["B4185", "B4187"]
    and the lipid dose of the beneficiary is justified.

rule pn_lipid_dosing with provenance LCD L38953,
        confer "lipid use per month in excess of the product-specific, FDA-approved dosing recommendations (B4185, B4187)":
the lipid dose of a beneficiary is justified
    if it is not the case that
        the lipid use of the beneficiary exceeds the FDA approved dosing recommendations
    otherwise the finding excess lipid dosing necessary about the beneficiary is established.

% the premix solutions and the additives: the caloric intake alone — a
% device of this model (the LCD sets no range of their own)
rule pn_premix_and_additives:
the nutrient order of an item is justified for a beneficiary
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["B4189", "B4193", "B4197", "B4199", "B4216"]
    and the item is furnished to the beneficiary.

rule pn_special_formulas with provenance LCD L38953,
        confer "The beneficiary’s medical record must adequately document the specific condition and the necessity for the special nutrient":
the nutrient order of an item is justified for a beneficiary
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["B5000", "B5100", "B5200"]
    and the item is furnished to the beneficiary
    and the finding special parenteral nutrient necessary about the beneficiary is established.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% The supply allowances and the pumps.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule pn_supply_allowance with provenance Policy Article A58836,
        confer "only one supply kit and one administration kit is covered for each day that parenteral nutrition is administered":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["B4220", "B4222", "B4224"]
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary meets the parenteral nutrition coverage criteria
    and the claim is within one parenteral supply allowance a day.

% one unit a day, a month read as 31 days
rule pn_allowance_daily with provenance Policy Article A58836,
        confer "Only one unit of service may be billed for any one day":
a claim is within one parenteral supply allowance a day
    if the claim is for a supply of a number months
    and the quantity billed on the claim is an other number
    and a limit is 31 * the number
    and the other number <= the limit.

rule pn_pump with provenance Policy Article A58836,
        confer "When parenteral nutrition is administered in an outpatient facility, the pump used for its administration and IV pole will be denied as not separately payable":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["B9004", "B9006"]
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary meets the parenteral nutrition coverage criteria
    and it is not the case that
        the beneficiary receives the parenteral nutrition in an outpatient facility.

section remedy is:

% The Policy Article's own conditions of payment: the test of permanence, no
% stay covered by Part A, and the LCD's dispensing cap.
rule pn_documentation with provenance Policy Article A58836,
        confer "In order to satisfy the test of permanence, there must be documentation to reflect that in the treating practitioner’s judgement, the impairment will be of long and indefinite duration":
the policy specific documentation requirements are met for a claim
    if the policy of the claim is parenteral_nutrition
    and the claim is for an item
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the finding permanent gastrointestinal impairment about the beneficiary is established
    and it is not the case that
        the beneficiary is in an inpatient stay covered by hospital insurance
    and the claim is within the dispensing limit for parenteral nutrition.

% (the stay: "No payment from Part B is available when parenteral nutrition
% services are furnished to a beneficiary in a stay covered by Part A")

rule pn_dispensing_limit with provenance LCD L38953,
        confer "No more than one month's supply of parenteral nutrients, equipment or supplies is allowed for one month's prospective billing":
a claim is within the dispensing limit for parenteral nutrition
    if the claim is for a supply of a number months
    and the number <= 1.

% the pump is equipment, not a supply: a device of this model
rule pn_pump_not_dispensed:
a claim is within the dispensing limit for parenteral nutrition
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["B9004", "B9006"].
